---
import run from '../../public/assets/benchmarks/hindsight-jev/live-results.json';

const { baseline, memory, combined } = run.summary;
---

<section class="takeaways-panel" aria-labelledby="takeaways">
  <div class="takeaways-overview">
    <div class="takeaways-message">
      <slot />
      <p class="takeaways-lead">Use recall when the answer depends on an earlier decision.</p>
      <p>The worker scored {baseline.correct}/{baseline.n} without history. Hindsight supplied the missing facts. Jev’s preflight gate held both repeats of one answerable lookup for review.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="takeaways-result">
      <p>Task completion in this run</p>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt>Hindsight alone</dt>
          <dd>{memory.correct}/{memory.n}</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt>Hindsight + Jev</dt>
          <dd>{combined.correct}/{combined.n}</dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </div>

  <div class="takeaways-guidance">
    <div>
      <h3>Hindsight for cross-session context</h3>
      <p>Store confirmed decisions with <code>remember</code>. Run <code>ask</code> with the same user and project to give the worker the relevant facts.</p>
      <p><strong>Skip recall</strong> when the request already contains the facts it needs. For current status, query the system that owns it.</p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Jev for drafts that apply constraints</h3>
      <p>Try <code>--jev</code> when a draft could violate a remembered constraint. In the controlled draft test, Jev with recall released 10/10 supported factual drafts and withheld 12/12 unsupported ones.</p>
      <p><strong>Skip the gate</strong> for straightforward lookups or checks your code can enforce directly, such as an allowlist.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .takeaways-panel {
    margin: 3rem 0;
    padding: clamp(1.25rem, 4vw, 2.25rem);
    border: 1px solid color-mix(in srgb, var(--memory-violet) 34%, var(--line));
    border-top: 4px solid var(--memory-violet);
    border-radius: .5rem;
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--memory-violet) 7%, var(--post-surface));
  }

  .takeaways-overview { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(12rem, .7fr); gap: 1.75rem; align-items: end; }
  .takeaways-panel .takeaways-message :global(h2) {
    margin: 0 0 .85rem;
    padding: 0;
    color: var(--memory-violet) !important;
    font-size: .78rem;
    letter-spacing: .12em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .takeaways-panel .takeaways-message :global(h2)::before { display: none; }
  .takeaways-panel p { margin: 0; font-size: .95rem; line-height: 1.6; }
  .takeaways-panel .takeaways-lead { margin: 0 0 .65rem; color: var(--post-heading); font-size: clamp(1.45rem, 3vw, 2.15rem); font-weight: 750; line-height: 1.15; text-wrap: balance; }

  .takeaways-result { border-inline-start: 1px solid var(--line); padding-inline-start: 1.25rem; }
  .takeaways-panel .takeaways-result p { margin-bottom: .65rem; color: var(--post-muted); font-size: .8rem; }
  .takeaways-result dl { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: .9rem; margin: 0; }
  .takeaways-result dt { color: var(--post-muted); font-size: .76rem; line-height: 1.35; }
  .takeaways-result dd { margin: .2rem 0 0; color: var(--post-heading); font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 3vw, 2rem); font-weight: 750; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; line-height: 1.1; }

  .takeaways-guidance { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1.5rem; padding-top: 1.25rem; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .takeaways-panel .takeaways-guidance h3 { margin: 0 0 .4rem; font-size: 1rem; font-weight: 700; }
  .takeaways-panel .takeaways-guidance p + p { margin-top: .65rem; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .takeaways-overview, .takeaways-guidance { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 1rem; }
    .takeaways-result { border-inline-start: 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); padding: 1rem 0 0; }
  }
</style>
